{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtzyRuA64BWZNM7d7F46vD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: rel03.1-uc001-uname\n2\ttitle: \"Print system information via uname\"\n3\t\n4\tsummary: |\n5\t  The operator invokes the Go uname binary to print system information fields such as\n6\t  kernel name, hostname, kernel release, version, and machine architecture. Individual\n7\t  flags select specific fields; -a prints all fields in canonical order. The differential\n8\t  testing harness runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (guname from\n9\t  coreutils) with the same flags and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n10\t\n11\tactor: Human Operator\n12\t\n13\ttrigger: |\n14\t  The operator has completed the PRD (srd044-uname.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n15\t  produce a passing differential test for cmd/uname.\n16\t\n17\tflow:\n18\t  - id: F1\n19\t    step: |\n20\t      Build cmd/uname via mage build. Requires no prior steps.\n21\t  - id: F2\n22\t    step: |\n23\t      Run ./bin/uname with each flag combination (default, -s, -n, -r, -v, -m, -p,\n24\t      -i, -o, -a). Requires F1 (binary must be built).\n25\t  - id: F3\n26\t    step: |\n27\t      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/uname and\n28\t      guname with identical flags and environment, comparing stdout byte-for-byte and\n29\t      exit codes. Requires F1 (binary must be built).\n30\t\n31\ttouchpoints:\n32\t  - T1: \"cmd/uname — system information output (srd044-uname R1, R2, R3)\"\n33\t  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout comparison\"\n34\t  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler\"\n35\t\n36\tsuccess_criteria:\n37\t  - id: S1\n38\t    criterion: |\n39\t      The differential test passes for all flag combinations (default, -s, -n, -r,\n40\t      -v, -m, -p, -i, -o, -a, and error cases), confirming full parity with guname.\n41\t    traces:\n42\t      - AC1\n43\t      - AC2\n44\t      - AC3\n45\t      - AC4\n46\t\n47\tout_of_scope:\n48\t  - Setting system information is not supported and not tested.\n49\t  - Long-form flag names beyond --help and --version are not tested.\n50\t\n51\ttest_suite: test-rel03.1\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7039a9e-9225-44ca-a28d-bff949cf7958","uuid":"7ae05061-e706-4d39-abfe-66a7a3db9770","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:32:15.217Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196/docs/specs/use-cases/rel03.1-uc001-uname.yaml","content":"id: rel03.1-uc001-uname\ntitle: \"Print system information via uname\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator invokes the Go uname binary to print system information fields such as\n  kernel name, hostname, kernel release, version, and machine architecture. Individual\n  flags select specific fields; -a prints all fields in canonical order. The differential\n  testing harness runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (guname from\n  coreutils) with the same flags and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (srd044-uname.yaml) and invokes do-work to\n  produce a passing differential test for cmd/uname.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      Build cmd/uname via mage build. Requires no prior steps.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      Run ./bin/uname with each flag combination (default, -s, -n, -r, -v, -m, -p,\n      -i, -o, -a). Requires F1 (binary must be built).\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/uname and\n      guname with identical flags and environment, comparing stdout byte-for-byte and\n      exit codes. Requires F1 (binary must be built).\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/uname — system information output (srd044-uname R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, stdout comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: |\n      The differential test passes for all flag combinations (default, -s, -n, -r,\n      -v, -m, -p, -i, -o, -a, and error cases), confirming full parity with guname.\n    traces:\n      - AC1\n      - AC2\n      - AC3\n      - AC4\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Setting system information is not supported and not tested.\n  - Long-form flag names beyond --help and --version are not tested.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel03.1\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
