{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a comprehensive stitch task (Task ID: 5196) to implement `cmd/uname/main.go` with core flags for the go-unix-utils project. The specific scope is srd044-uname requirements R1.1-R1.4 only:\n   - R1.1: Default behavior (no args) prints kernel name + newline, exit 0\n   - R1.2: `-s` flag prints kernel name (e.g., Darwin, Linux)\n   - R1.3: `-n` flag prints network node hostname\n   - R1.4: `-r` flag prints kernel release string\n   \n   The task is part of a cobbler-scaffold generation pipeline (Run 44) on branch `task/generation-run44-5196`. Git is managed externally — no git commands allowed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **syscall.Uname**: Design decision D1 specifies using `syscall.Uname` to obtain the `Utsname` struct, converting fixed-size int8/byte arrays to Go strings by scanning for null terminator\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main (project convention for all cmd/ utilities)\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Uses `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing against `guname` (Homebrew GNU reference binary)\n   - **SRD non_goals conflict**: The SRD explicitly states \"cmd/uname does not support long-form flag names beyond --help and --version\" — this conflicts with design decision D2 which mentions `--kernel-name`. Per execution constitution article E6, non_goals take precedence, so only short flags (-s, -n, -r) should be implemented\n   - **Extensible flag-to-field mapping**: D4 requires structuring code so additional flags (R1.5-R1.9 for -v, -m, -p, -i, -o) can be added later without restructuring\n   - **Copyright header**: Every Go file must start with `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` and `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - **Function size limit**: 40 lines hard limit (E8)\n   - **Build command**: `go build -o bin/uname ./cmd/uname/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd044-uname.yaml** (READ)\n     - Full SRD for uname utility with R1 (individual flags R1.1-R1.9), R2 (combined output -a), R3 (error handling), R4 (differential testing)\n     - Only R1.1-R1.4 are in scope for this task\n     - Critical non_goals: \"cmd/uname does not support long-form flag names beyond --help and --version\"\n     - Key requirements text:\n       - R1.1: \"When invoked with no arguments, must print the kernel name (equivalent to -s) followed by a newline and exit 0.\"\n       - R1.2: \"-s must print the kernel name (e.g., Darwin, Linux).\"\n       - R1.3: \"-n must print the network node hostname.\"\n       - R1.4: \"-r must print the kernel release string.\"\n\n   - **docs/specs/use-cases/rel03.1-uc001-uname.yaml** (READ)\n     - Use case describing the operator invoking uname with various flags\n     - Touchpoints: cmd/uname (srd044-uname R1, R2, R3), pkg/testutils (RunDiffTests), pkg/sys (InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n     - Reference binary: guname from Homebrew coreutils\n\n   - **cmd/uname/main.go** (TO BE CREATED)\n     - The sole file to create for this task\n     - Must implement package main with sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler(), flag parsing for -s/-n/-r, and syscall.Uname-based system info retrieval\n\n   - **pkg/sys** (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT - contract only)\n     - Exports: `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` with signature `func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n     - Import path: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - **pkg/testutils** (PROVIDED IN CONTEXT - contract only)  \n     - Exports: `BuildBinary`, `RunDiffTests`, `DiffTest` struct\n     - Used in test files (not in scope for this task since only main.go is listed)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet — only two file reads were completed before the