{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dvv7oKH2SJWZ3eAEwm9jQV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\tpackage sys\n5\t\n6\timport (\n7\t\t\"os\"\n8\t\t\"os/signal\"\n9\t\t\"sync\"\n10\t\t\"syscall\"\n11\t)\n12\t\n13\tvar (\n14\t\tresizeMu        sync.Mutex\n15\t\tresizeCallbacks  []func(width int)\n16\t\tresizeSetupOnce  sync.Once\n17\t)\n18\t\n19\t// OnTerminalResize registers a callback invoked with the new terminal width\n20\t// when a SIGWINCH signal is received.\n21\t// R3.1: calls TerminalWidth() on SIGWINCH and invokes callback with the new width.\n22\t// R3.2: supports multiple callbacks called in registration order.\n23\tfunc OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) {\n24\t\tresizeMu.Lock()\n25\t\tresizeCallbacks = append(resizeCallbacks, callback)\n26\t\tresizeMu.Unlock()\n27\t\n28\t\tresizeSetupOnce.Do(startResizeListener)\n29\t}\n30\t\n31\tfunc startResizeListener() {\n32\t\tc := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n33\t\tsignal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGWINCH)\n34\t\tgo handleResizeSignals(c)\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\tfunc handleResizeSignals(c <-chan os.Signal) {\n38\t\tfor range c {\n39\t\t\twidth, err := TerminalWidth()\n40\t\t\tif err != nil {\n41\t\t\t\tcontinue\n42\t\t\t}\n43\t\t\tresizeMu.Lock()\n44\t\t\tcbs := make([]func(int), len(resizeCallbacks))\n45\t\t\tcopy(cbs, resizeCallbacks)\n46\t\t\tresizeMu.Unlock()\n47\t\t\tfor _, cb := range cbs {\n48\t\t\t\tcb(width)\n49\t\t\t}\n50\t\t}\n51\t}\n52\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HfRRCAWT4W954bQkePgNDG","session_id":"f7039a9e-9225-44ca-a28d-bff949