{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HfRRCAWT4W954bQkePgNDG","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've explored the codebase patterns in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196` and found excellent examples of manual POSIX-style flag parsing. Here are my findings:\n\n### Example 1: Simple Utility (hostname)\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196/cmd/hostname/main.go`\n\nThis is a straightforward example showing:\n- Manual flag parsing with a for loop over `os.Args[1:]`\n- Switch statement handling `--help`, `--version`, and `--` (argument terminator)\n- String prefix checking for flag validation with `strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\")`\n- Use of `goto done` for control flow to exit the flag parsing loop\n- Proper error handling with stderr output and exit codes\n- Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at the start\n\n### Example 2: Complex Utility with Options (seq)\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196/cmd/seq/main.go`\n\nThis demonstrates more sophisticated manual flag parsing:\n- An `options` struct to hold parsed flags\n- `parseArgs()` function that handles:\n  - Long flags with `--` prefix (both `--format=VALUE` and `--format VALUE` styles)\n  - Short flags with `-` prefix and combining multiple short flags\n  - Proper detection of negative numbers vs. flags using `isNumStart()`\n  - The `--` terminator for stopping flag parsing\n- Separate helper functions: `parseLongFlag()`, `parseShortFlags()`\n- Manual argument consumption tracking (returns number of args consumed)\n- Returns a tuple: `(options, []string, error)` where the slice is remaining operands\n\n### syscall.Uname Usage\nThe codebase **does not use `syscall.Uname`**. Instead, it uses:\n- `os.Hostname()` for hostname\n- `syscall.Sysctl(\"hw.machine\")` for machine architecture (in arch/main.go)\n\n### pkg/sys Package - InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n**Function Signature:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n- Creates a buffered channel: `c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)`\n- Calls `signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)` to trap SIGPIPE signals\n- Spawns a goroutine that exits with code 0 when signal is received\n- Safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine\n- Matches GNU coreutils behavior: process exits cleanly when stdout/stderr is closed by a downstream consumer\n\n**Related pkg/sys Functions:**\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - registers callbacks for SIGWINCH signals\n- Functions in `terminal.go`, `stat_darwin.go`, and `fileinfo.go` provide Unix utilities\n\nThe pattern used throughout is **manual POSIX-style flag parsing without the standard `flag` package**, giving fine-grained control over argument handling and error reporting."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7039a9e-9225-44ca-a28d-bff949cf7958","uuid":"633e6e69-bbce-43fd-a207-c41ba09733fb","timestamp":"2026-05-14T17:33:59.304Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196, I need to understand patterns used in existing cmd/ implementations. Find a cmd/ directory that has a main.go with flag parsing (especially manual/POSIX-style flag parsing, not using the standard \"flag\" package). Show me 1-2 examples of complete main.go files from cmd/ directories, prioritizing simple ones like hostname, whoami, or similar single-purpose utilities. Also show me how syscall.Uname is used if any file uses it. Also check what the pkg/sys package looks like - specifically the InstallSIGPIPEHandler function signature.","agentId":"a6b3689e4c58bc107","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've explored the codebase patterns in `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196` and found excellent examples of manual POSIX-style flag parsing. Here are my findings:\n\n### Example 1: Simple Utility (hostname)\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196/cmd/hostname/main.go`\n\nThis is a straightforward example showing:\n- Manual flag parsing with a for loop over `os.Args[1:]`\n- Switch statement handling `--help`, `--version`, and `--` (argument terminator)\n- String prefix checking for flag validation with `strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\")`\n- Use of `goto done` for control flow to exit the flag parsing loop\n- Proper error handling with stderr output and exit codes\n- Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at the start\n\n### Example 2: Complex Utility with Options (seq)\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196/cmd/seq/main.go`\n\nThis demonstrates more sophisticated manual flag parsing:\n- An `options` struct to hold parsed flags\n- `parseArgs()` function that handles:\n  - Long flags with `--` prefix (both `--format=VALUE` and `--format VALUE` styles)\n  - Short flags with `-` prefix and combining multiple short flags\n  - Proper detection of negative numbers vs. flags using `isNumStart()`\n  - The `--` terminator for stopping flag parsing\n- Separate helper functions: `parseLongFlag()`, `parseShortFlags()`\n- Manual argument consumption tracking (returns number of args consumed)\n- Returns a tuple: `(options, []string, error)` where the slice is remaining operands\n\n### syscall.Uname Usage\nThe codebase **does not use `syscall.Uname`**. Instead, it uses:\n- `os.Hostname()` for hostname\n- `syscall.Sysctl(\"hw.machine\")` for machine architecture (in arch/main.go)\n\n### pkg/sys Package - InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5196/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\n**Function Signature:**\n```go\nfunc InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n```\n\n**Implementation Details:**\n- Creates a buffered channel: `c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)`\n- Calls `signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)` to trap SIGPIPE signals\n- Spawns a goroutine that exits with code 0 when signal is received\n- Safe to call multiple times; each invocation starts one goroutine\n- Matches GNU coreutils behavior: process exits cleanly when stdout/stderr is closed by a downstream consumer\n\n**Related pkg/sys Functions:**\n- `OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))` - registers callbacks for SIGWINCH signals\n- Functions in `terminal.go`, `stat_darwin.go`, and `fileinfo.go` provide Unix utilities\n\nThe pattern used throughout is **manual POSIX-style flag parsing without the standard `flag` package**, giving fine-grained control over argument handling and error reporting."}],"totalDurationMs":35407,"totalTokens":28646,"totalToolUseCount":14,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_read_input_tokens":27028,"output_tokens":895,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":719},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":895,"cache_read_input_tokens":27028,"cache_creation_input_tokens":719,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":719,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":5,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":7,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
