and. That matches guname behavior.\n\nLet me verify: `guname -` should give \"extra operand\" error.\nActually, no. Let me think again. `-` is a single character. Does guname treat it as an operand?\n\nActually I realize I don't need to test edge cases not in scope. R1.1-R1.4 are what matter. Let me just write the code.\n\nI need to check whether the `cmd/uname/` directory exists or if the Write tool will create it automatically.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2742,"cache_read_input_tokens":30122,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2742},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7039a9e-9225-44ca-a28d-bff949cf7958","uuid":"135f0707-d94d-4120-b8b6-7479adc6caac"}
